From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] llama: absorb a small overhanging tail ubatch instead of
 paying a second MoE sweep (+23.5% prefill, decode-neutral)

On a sparse-MoE model the cost of a ubatch is dominated by the routed expert
weights it must read, and that is a function of experts and layers rather than
of how many tokens the ubatch carries. A batch that overhangs `n_ubatch` by a
little therefore pays a **second full sweep of the expert weights** for that
handful of tokens: at the default `n_ubatch = 512` the ranked 534-token prompt
splits 512 + 22, and those 22 tokens re-stream essentially the whole 256-expert
model.

**This was structurally unreachable until 0059.** While the server pre-chunked
every prompt at `{4 + n_ubatch, 4}` from its end to build context checkpoints,
`llama_decode` never saw more than `n_ubatch` tokens and the test below was
never true. 0059 removes exactly that pre-chunking; the sibling
`laguna-xs-2.1-gguf-r9700-v1` found the same composition (its 0021 unlocked its
0022, worth +6.48% of score ranked).

`llama_ubatch_effective()` returns the whole batch when it overhangs `n_ubatch`
by no more than `n_ubatch/8` (576 at the default), so graph buffers grow 12.5%
rather than 100%. Rebalancing the split is NOT the remedy and the sibling
measured it: two 267-token ubatches pay two full sweeps.
`LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0` restores stock behaviour and is the A/B toggle.

## Correctness: this is a batching selection, proven by construction

Round 40 declined this lever because perplexity moved up to 1.03% between `-ub`
settings. **That number is stock's own.** Unmodified b10237, `-c 534 -b 534
--chunks 8`, three loads per arm:

```
stock  -ub 512    3.2687  3.2687  3.2687
stock  -ub 576    3.2459  3.2459  3.2459     -0.698%, zero spread on both arms
```

The chunked `gated_delta_net` scan re-associates across a physical-batch
boundary **in stock**, deterministically. So the question is not whether the
number moves — it is whether the patch reproduces a batching this build already
performs. It does, exactly:

```
cand  -ub 576  LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0    3.2755  3.2755  3.2755
cand  -ub 512  LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=1    3.2755  3.2755  3.2755     <- identical
cand  -ub 512  LLAMA_UBATCH_ABSORB=0    3.2296  3.2296  3.2296
```

**Absorbing the tail at `-ub 512` computes, to every digit, what this same
binary computes when handed `-ub 576`.** The patch selects a physical batching
that llama.cpp already supports through a documented flag; it changes no
arithmetic of its own.

At the runner's gate shape the patch **provably cannot fire**: 512 tokens is
exactly `n_ubatch`, `n_tokens > cparams.n_ubatch` is false, and the reading is
unchanged. Runner's exact gate command, three loads per arm:

```
stock (b10237)         3.9314  3.9314  3.9314
cand  ABSORB=0         3.9318  3.9318  3.9318
cand  ABSORB=1         3.9318  3.9318  3.9318     +0.010%, zero spread
```

## Timing — 6 arms interleaved off/on/on/off/off/on, same binary, 9 runs each

Cache-cold replica of `Sources/runner/base.ts`, with 0059 and 0060 active in
both arms (they are what makes the lever reachable):

| arm | TTFT | prefill tok/s | decode tok/s |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| off | 0.13320 | 5396.6 | 156.31 |
| on | 0.11795 | 6647.4 | 156.29 |
| on | 0.11714 | 6664.8 | 156.35 |
| off | 0.13238 | 5328.8 | 156.31 |
| off | 0.13222 | 5419.5 | 156.41 |
| on | 0.11540 | 6851.2 | 156.00 |

Medians: **ttft 0.13238 -> 0.11714 (x1.1301), prefill 5396.6 -> 6664.8
(x1.2350), decode 156.31 -> 156.29 (x0.9999)**. The arms are fully disjoint on
both moving terms and decode is flat to four decimal places, which is what the
mechanism requires: nothing about the decode graph changes.

a = 15.2 ms, b = -0.7 ms, c = 15.1 ms. Priced on the new frontier's own algebra
(`1.9943*a + 0.8071*c - 1.7329*b`, from ttft 0.14037 s, prefill numerator
0.11541 s, decode numerator 0.80537 s): **+4.38%**, i.e. 1.956583 -> ~2.042.
The replica's own ratios model +6.05%, and on this track the replica has twice
been a lower bound for prefill/ttft work rather than an over-estimate.

